  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Breathing Text\n\nLetters flex between two variable-font settings (weight and slant) in a staggered, mirrored loop, so the word appears to breathe.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 6 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A word or short phrase should stay alive on screen by pulsing between thin and heavy letterforms.\n- The type is a variable font and the weight or slant axis is the point of the shot.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You want a single decisive weight change that lands once: use variable-axis-type or variable-font-flex.\n- The text must hold perfectly still while it is read.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"breathing text\"\n- font_size (number, 24-400): Font size, default 120\n- color (color): Color, default \"#111111\"\n- from_weight (number, 100-1000): From weight, default 100\n- to_weight (number, 100-1000): To weight, default 800\n- from_slant (number, -10-0): From slant, default 0\n- to_slant (number, -10-0): To slant, default -10\n- breath_duration (number, 0.2-6): Breath duration, default 1.5\n- stagger (number, 0-0.5): Stagger, default 0.08\n- stagger_from (enum): Stagger from, default \"first\"\n- repeat_delay (number, 0-2): Repeat delay, default 0.1\n\nSource: https://github.com/danielpetho/fancy. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
